<div class="disclosures daily-checks">
  <details><summary>Backups &amp; failed jobs</summary><div><p>A successful backup job alone does not prove a tested restore. In a review, a failed job is a question to investigate, not an explanation of the cause.</p><p><strong>What to ask:</strong> What failed, what needs another check, and who owns the follow-up?</p></div></details>
  <details><summary>Alerts &amp; system health</summary><div><p>A warning needs the context of the affected system and the work that depends on it. An alert count alone does not show the business impact.</p><p><strong>What to ask:</strong> Is this a new signal, a recurring issue or an action already under investigation?</p></div></details>
  <details><summary>Open work &amp; follow-up</summary><div><p>A review can connect an open question with the next action and the information needed to continue it.</p><p><strong>What to ask:</strong> What is waiting, who owns it, and what would let it move forward?</p></div></details>
</div>
